  "cause": {
    "summary": "scene.support was hardcoded false in every run script, so the table/support collision geometry was never added to the scene. The object falls at reset and the episode terminates on frame ~0 for any clip that rests on a surface.",
    "evidence": [
      "brev/run_ab350.sh:53, brev/run_full350.sh:48, brev/run_tier1_backup.sh:67 all pass scene.support=false",
      "NVIDIA's configs/scene/train.yaml and eval.yaml default to support: true",
      "e03 and e09 report bit-identical add_auc at all 7 checkpoints (constant-error signature): 0.005601792573623559 and 0.0047413793103448275",
      "termination_cause_fraction object=1.0 and wrist=1.0 at every e03/e09 checkpoint",
      "e03 support USDA declares 1 Cylinder, top at 0.7573 + 0.04/2 = 0.7773 m, matching the 77.7 cm object rest height measured from the reference",
      "e18 (and e24) are floor clips whose released support USDA is the empty 125-byte stage, so support=false was already correct for them -- which is why they are the clips that learned"
    ],
    "scope": "14 of 30 Tier 2 clips ship support_surface primitives. The same bug explains the ~12 near-zero clips in the submitted Tier 1 entry.",
    "fix": "per clip, scene.support=true iff that clip's support USDA declares primitives, the rule brev/gate_on_instance.sh support_flag_for already implemented"
  },
